# Fallow compliance

Pre-commit runs `npm run fallow:precommit` (`scripts/fallow-precommit.mjs`):

1. Full-repo `fallow dead-code --fail-on-issues`
2. Staged-diff `fallow audit --fail-on-issues` (new issues only)

## When writing or moving code

- **Wire new modules from a reachable entry** (page, route, layout, barrel imported by those, worker, test). A file that nothing imports is an unused file and fails the hook.
- **Do not leave orphan refactors.** If you move/rename a component (e.g. `UploadModelWizard` → `upload-model-wizard/`), update every consumer in the same change or delete the old path and unused siblings.
- **Export only what callers need.** Prefer `function` / `type` over `export function` / `export type` until a second module imports it. Re-export barrels (`index.ts`) must not re-export unused symbols.
- **Delete superseded duplicates** instead of keeping parallel helpers (e.g. old `mapNavigatorStyle` after `bimMapNavigator`).
- **Do not add unused API wrappers** “for later.” Add the client helper when the UI/route calls it.
- **Class members:** if fallow false-positives a public method that is called (common with optional chaining), suppress with `// fallow-ignore-next-line unused-class-member` (or combine: `complexity, unused-class-member`). Prefer real usage over suppressions.
- **Suppressions are last resort.** Prefer delete, un-export, or wire-up. Never suppress an entire unfinished feature folder to ship dead code.

## Config notes (`.fallowrc.json`)

- `health.maxCrap: 400` — without coverage, estimated CRAP ≈ cyclomatic²; keep this ≥ `maxCyclomatic²` so CRAP does not fail every small branchy function.
- `duplicates.minLines: 20` — ignore tiny/boilerplate clones; still extract real shared logic above that size.
- Pre-commit also runs `fallow audit` on the staged diff (`gate: new-only`).

## Complexity suppressions

Prefer extracting helpers. When a function must stay complex, place the ignore **immediately above the function/arrow**:

```ts
// fallow-ignore-next-line complexity
export function BigComponent() { ... }

{items.map(
  // fallow-ignore-next-line complexity
  (item) => { ... },
)}
```

Never put `// fallow-ignore-…` as a raw JSX child (it renders as text and does not suppress).

## Before finishing a change that adds TS/TSX

```bash
npx fallow dead-code --quiet --fail-on-issues
# with staged changes:
npm run fallow:precommit
```
